          "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category. There exists a big category\n<MATH_0002> of <TEXTITOPEN_0001>pro-objects<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0003>.\nNamely, if <MATH_0004> and\n<MATH_0005> are cofiltered diagrams in <MATH_0006>,\nthen we can define\n<MATH_0007>\nThere is a canonical functor <MATH_0008>\nwhich maps <MATH_0009> to the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>constant system<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> on <MATH_0010>. This is a fully\nfaithful embedding. In this language one sees that a diagram <MATH_0011> is\nessentially constant if and only if <MATH_0012> is isomorphic to a constant system.\nIf we ever need this material, then we will formulate this into a lemma\nand prove it here.\n",
